    We set Pk for the set of polynomials of k−1 variables. We introduce partial
ordering in Pk in the following manner: we say that P1 ≺ P2 , P1 , P2 ∈ Pk ,
if and only if P1 ≤ P2 on Ak . This is inherited from the partial ordering
of functions of k − 1 variables on Ak defined as f ≺ g ⇐⇒ f ≤ g on Ak .
Furthermore, we consider
