   We proceed to prove our main result concerning the number of maximal
elements in Ak .
   Theorem 3.6. Let (un )n≥0 be the renewal masses of the random walk S
defined above. For k ≥ 3 there is no largest element in Ak .
   Given that Ak , k ≥ 3, has no largest element we formulate the following:
   Conjecture 3.7. For any k ≥ 3, Qk is a maximal element in Ak and it is
largest in Âk .
   In the direction of Conjecture 3.7 we prove a weaker version of it.
   Proposition 3.8. Conjecture 3.7 is valid for k = 3.

