H := P − Q3 and note that on ∂A3 , Q3 = m3 . Therefore, on ∂A3 we have
that H ≤ 0. Note that 4Det(H) = 4(a − 1)c − (b − 1)2 = −(a − c − 1)2
and as it is well-known if Det(H) ≤ 0, then maxG H = max∂G H ( and
minG H = min∂G H) for each bounded region G in the plane. Therefore,
P ≤ Q3 on A3 and the claim that Q3 is largest in Â3 is established.                □

